      "name": "GPIO4",
      "label": "GPIO4 (Button)",
      "codeName": "4",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "BOOTSEL button — on Revision D and later boards only, wired in parallel with the BOOTSEL bootloader-select circuit for use as a normal input; unconnected on earlier revisions (safe no-op there). No alias exists in this board's pins_arduino.h. Confirmed via Adafruit's own learn.adafruit.com pinouts guide (\"On Revision D and later of the Feather RP2040, the BOOTSEL button is connected to GPIO4 for use in your code\") and CircuitPython's current pins.c (BUTTON/BOOT -> GPIO4). Active-low with internal pull-up assumed by convention (matches adafruit_feather_scorpio GPIO7 / adafruit_itsybitsy GPIO13 BOOT buttons), not independently Zephyr-confirmed for this exact pin.\nCheck if available on board"
    },
